{"name":"Malibu","hex":"#66b7e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Malibu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Los Angeles County, California, United States, known for its beaches.","Ellipsis of Malibu Bay (“California”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of Malibu bay breeze","Alternative form of malibu"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Malibu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Malibu, California","blocks":[{"text":"Malibu is a beach city in the Santa Monica Mountains region of Los Angeles County, California, United States, about 30 miles (48 km) west of Los Angeles. It is known for its Mediterranean climate, its strip of beaches stretching 21 miles (34 km) along the Pacific coast, and for its longtime status as the home of numerous Hollywood celebrities and executives with several of its residents in the entertainment industry. The Pacific Coast Highway traverses the city, following along the South Coast of California. As of the 2020 census, the city's population was 10,654. The 2025 Palisades Fire devastated Malibu, with almost all of the beachfront homes in the east of the city being destroyed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/MalibuAir.jpg/330px-MalibuAir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malibu%2C_California","wikidata":"Q387047"},{"title":"Malibu High School","blocks":[{"text":"Malibu High School (MHS) is a public high school in Malibu, California. The school is one of three high schools in the Santa Monica–Malibu Unified School District and serves students in the city of Malibu and surrounding communities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Malibu_High_School_quad.jpg/330px-Malibu_High_School_quad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malibu_High_School","wikidata":"Q6743399"},{"title":"Malibu (rum)","blocks":[{"text":"Malibu is a coconut flavoured liqueur made with white rum, which has an alcohol content by volume of 21.0%. Since 2005 the Malibu brand has been owned by Pernod Ricard, which calls it a \"flavored rum\", where this designation is allowed by local laws."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/Malibu_%28rum%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malibu_(rum)","wikidata":"Q177092"},{"title":"Malibu (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Malibu is the second studio album by American singer Anderson .Paak. It was released on January 15, 2016, by ArtClub International, Empire Distribution, OBE and Steel Wool Records following the release of his EP, Link Up & Suede, with Knxwledge."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Anderson-Park-Malibu-Cover-Billboard-650x650.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malibu_(album)","wikidata":"Q21780585"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Seal_of_Malibu%2C_California.png/500px-Seal_of_Malibu%2C_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Seal_of_Malibu%2C_California.png/500px-Seal_of_Malibu%2C_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeal_of_Malibu%2C_California.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Adamson_House.JPG/500px-Adamson_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Adamson_House.JPG/1280px-Adamson_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki